{"format":1,"manifest":{"name":"git-commit-snippets","publisher":"vyloxi","version":"1.0.0","displayName":"Git Commit Templates","description":"Conventional Commit messages, merge and revert messages, issue references and a PR description template.","engines":{"ferrum":"^0.1.0"},"categories":["Snippets"],"icon":"icon.png","repository":"https://github.com/voukengdongmofrankysteve/ferrum-market","license":"MIT","contributes":{"snippets":[{"language":"*","path":"snippets/.json"}]}},"files":{"icon.png":{"encoding":"base64","content":""},"snippets/.json":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"{\n  \"feat\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"gc-feat\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"feat(${1:scope}): ${2:add something}\",\n      \"\",\n      \"${3:Why this change.}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A feature commit\"\n  },\n  \"fix\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"gc-fix\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"fix(${1:scope}): ${2:correct something}\",\n      \"\",\n      \"${3:What was wrong and how it is fixed.}\",\n      \"\",\n      \"Fixes #${4:123}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A fix commit\"\n  },\n  \"docs\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"gc-docs\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"docs(${1:scope}): ${2:update the guide}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A docs commit\"\n  },\n  \"style\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"gc-style\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"style(${1:scope}): ${2:format code}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A formatting commit\"\n  },\n  \"refactor\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"gc-refactor\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"refactor(${1:scope}): ${2:simplify something}\",\n      \"\",\n      \"No change in behavior.\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A refactor commit\"\n  },\n  \"perf\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"gc-perf\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"perf(${1:scope}): ${2:speed up something}\",\n      \"\",\n      \"${3:Before and after numbers.}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A performance commit\"\n  },\n  \"test\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"gc-test\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"test(${1:scope}): ${2:cover the edge case}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A test commit\"\n  },\n  \"build\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"gc-build\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"build(${1:deps}): ${2:bump a dependency}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A build commit\"\n  },\n  \"ci\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"gc-ci\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"ci: ${1:update the workflow}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A CI commit\"\n  },\n  \"chore\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"gc-chore\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"chore: ${1:housekeeping}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A chore commit\"\n  },\n  \"revert\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"gc-revert\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"revert: ${1:feat(scope): the original subject}\",\n      \"\",\n      \"This reverts commit ${2:abcdef0}.\",\n      \"\",\n      \"Reason: ${3:why}.\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A revert commit\"\n  },\n  \"breaking change\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"gc-break\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"${1:feat}(${2:scope})!: ${3:change the API}\",\n      \"\",\n      \"BREAKING CHANGE: ${4:what breaks and how to migrate.}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A breaking change\"\n  },\n  \"merge\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"gc-merge\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"Merge branch '${1:feature}' into ${2:main}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A merge commit\"\n  },\n  \"wip\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"gc-wip\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"wip: ${1:checkpoint}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A work in progress commit\"\n  },\n  \"co-author\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"gc-co\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"Co-authored-by: ${1:Name} <${2:email@example.com}>\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A co-author trailer\"\n  },\n  \"PR description\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"gc-pr\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"## What\",\n      \"${1:What changed.}\",\n      \"\",\n      \"## Why\",\n      \"${2:Why it is needed.}\",\n      \"\",\n      \"## How to test\",\n      \"1. ${3:Step one}\",\n      \"\",\n      \"## Checklist\",\n      \"- [ ] Tests added\",\n      \"- [ ] Docs updated\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A pull request description\"\n  },\n  \"Issue report\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"gc-issue\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"## Summary\",\n      \"${1:What went wrong.}\",\n      \"\",\n      \"## Steps to reproduce\",\n      \"1. ${2:Step}\",\n      \"\",\n      \"## Expected\",\n      \"${3:What should happen.}\",\n      \"\",\n      \"## Actual\",\n      \"${4:What happens.}\",\n      \"\",\n      \"## Environment\",\n      \"- Version: ${5}\",\n      \"- OS: ${6}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A bug report\"\n  }\n}\n"},"README.md":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"# Git Commit Templates\n\nConventional Commit messages, merge and revert messages, issue references and a PR description template.\n\nType a prefix and press Tab. 17 snippets.\n\n| Language | Prefix | What it inserts |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| * | `gc-feat` | A feature commit |\n| * | `gc-fix` | A fix commit |\n| * | `gc-docs` | A docs commit |\n| * | `gc-style` | A formatting commit |\n| * | `gc-refactor` | A refactor commit |\n| * | `gc-perf` | A performance commit |\n| * | `gc-test` | A test commit |\n| * | `gc-build` | A build commit |\n| * | `gc-ci` | A CI commit |\n| * | `gc-chore` | A chore commit |\n| * | `gc-revert` | A revert commit |\n| * | `gc-break` | A breaking change |\n| * | `gc-merge` | A merge commit |\n| * | `gc-wip` | A work in progress commit |\n| * | `gc-co` | A co-author trailer |\n| * | `gc-pr` | A pull request description |\n| * | `gc-issue` | A bug report |\n\nThis extension runs no code and asks for no permissions.\n"}}}